# GitHub CLI binary (kept in .girignore as a manual mirror)
gh.exe

# P1: generated data + runtime logs (out of git)
#   - logs/ is the runtime log tree — fully regenerated per run
#   - gnosis-training/data/*.jsonl are the templated training sets,
#     regenerated by generate_pairs.py + scripts/expand_seeded_g2.py etc.
#   The 99 MB of historical blobs stays in history (rewrite is a
#   separate, riskier job). Nothing new accumulates; fresh clones stay
#   small. The single existing carve-out
#   (!monad-ecosystem/packages/hcd-monitor/tests/fixtures/*.jsonl)
#   is upstream of this rule and unaffected.
# Runtime logs are ignored, but git must still descend into logs/ so the
# build inputs below can be re-included. `logs/` (directory form) would
# stop traversal and make the negations below unreachable.
logs/*
!logs/corpus/
logs/corpus/*
# BUILD INPUT, not a runtime log: control-center's build-corpus.js reads
# this at build time to generate public/logoc-corpus.json. Untracking it
# in P1 broke `pnpm build` for the frontend from a clean clone.
!logs/corpus/master_corpus_v5.10.jsonl
gnosis-training/data/*.jsonl

# Local Claude Code session data (plans, worktrees, settings) — never commit
.claude/

scripts/node_modules/
scripts/package-lock.json
scripts/package.json
scripts/meshaleach-shots/

